---
title: Adult Mac and Cheese
description: 'Our creamy stovetop mac and cheese is about as easy as opening a box—and a whooooole lot more delicious. '
image: https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5cacf0e37fbac95e35dcc499/16:9/w_7520,h_4230,c_limit/basically-adult-mac-and-cheese-2-21022019.jpg
servings: 4
yield: 4 servings
source: https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/adult-mac-and-cheese
author: Molly Baz
tags: mac and cheese, parmesan, pasta shells, easy, quick, one-pot meals, weeknight meals, 5 ingredients or fewer, main, nut-free, vegetarian, simmer, dinner, basically, web
---

Add a big handful of @kosher salt{} to a large #pot{} of water and bring to a boil. 

Drop @shells{1%lb} into boiling water and give them a good stir to be sure nothing sticks. Set a timer according to package directions for al dente.

Cut @butter{½%cup}(chilled unsalted) into 8 pieces.

While pasta is cooking, heat @butter{2%Tbsp} and @ground black pepper{2%tsp} in a large heavy #pot{} or Dutch oven over medium, stirring occasionally, until butter is melted and foaming, but not browned, and pepper is fragrant, about 1 minute.

Add @whole milk{1%cup} to butter to stop it from browning and bring to a simmer. Whisk remaining @butter{6%Tbsp} into milk mixture 1 Tbsp. at a time, allowing each to fully melt before adding the next. You may need to adjust your heat occasionally to maintain a simmer. If pasta still needs a few more minutes to cook, turn off heat under your sauce, cover pot, and keep warm.

Scoop up @pasta cooking liquid{2%cups} with a large glass measuring cup. You're probably not going to use all of the pasta water in your sauce, but it's better to have more than you'll need.

Drain pasta and add to pot with milk mixture. Return to medium heat and cook, tossing with a wooden spoon to evenly coat all shells, about 30 seconds.

Add about one-third of @Parmesan{5%oz}, stirring pasta vigorously with a wooden spoon to melt. Add about @pasta cooking liquid{½%cup} and continue to stir until combined. Repeat this process 2 more times with remaining Parmesan. You may not need all of the pasta water, so add @pasta cooking liquid{½%cup} at a time until pasta is very creamy and well coated. It’s always good to err on the side of looser because the sauce will thicken as it cools. Give it a taste and add more @kosher salt{} if needed.

Divide pasta between bowls—or just heap it into one big bowl for yourself, no judgie—and serve right away.